A host that reads the list through lab-mail needs an mbsync config to
sync it and an msmtp config to post to it. Every host's differs only
in the login, so one documented sample of each serves them all, and
no host's own values ship in the package.

- The mbsync sample is for a login that may write the list, so it
  syncs both ways and expunges on both sides. It says how a read-only
  login differs.
- PassCmd reads the password from a file only the user can read, so
  the config holds no secret and can be kept in the repo as it is.
  lab-mail's spec and README said Pat keeps his password in pass(1),
  which he does not use; they now name that file.
- README.org gives the commands to set up a login, sync, and post.
